`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Distributed mode can be subdivided into distributed but all daemons run on a single node — a.k.a. ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"pseudo-distributed"})," — and ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"fully-distributed"})," where the daemons are spread across all nodes in the cluster. The ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"pseudo-distributed"})," vs. ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"fully-distributed"})," nomenclature comes from Hadoop."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Pseudo-distributed mode can run against the local filesystem or it can run against an instance of the ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"Hadoop Distributed File System"})," (HDFS). Fully-distributed mode can ONLY run on HDFS. See the Hadoop ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://hadoop.apache.org/docs/current/",children:"documentation"})," for how to set up HDFS. A good walk-through for setting up HDFS on Hadoop 2 can be found at ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://web.archive.org/web/20221007121526/https://www.alexjf.net/blog/distributed-systems/hadoop-yarn-installation-definitive-guide/",children:"https://web.archive.org/web/20221007121526/https://www.alexjf.net/blog/distributed-systems/hadoop-yarn-installation-definitive-guide/"}),"."]}),`
