`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:[e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Description:"})," The max number of concurrent pending requests for one server in all client threads (process level). Exceeding requests will be thrown ServerTooBusyException immediately to prevent user's threads being occupied and blocked by only one slow region server. If you use a fix number of threads to access HBase in a synchronous way, set this to a suitable value which is related to the number of threads will help you. See ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/HBASE-16388",children:"https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/HBASE-16388"})," for details.",e.jsx(i.br,{}),`
`,e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Default:"})," ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"2147483647"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(i.h4,{id:"hbaseclientscannercaching-toc",children:e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.client.scanner.caching"})}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:[e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Description:"})," Number of rows that we try to fetch when calling next on a scanner if it is not served from (local, client) memory. This configuration works together with hbase.client.scanner.max.result.size to try and use the network efficiently. The default value is Integer.MAX_VALUE by default so that the network will fill the chunk size defined by hbase.client.scanner.max.result.size rather than be limited by a particular number of rows since the size of rows varies table to table. If you know ahead of time that you will not require more than a certain number of rows from a scan, this configuration should be set to that row limit via Scan#setCaching. Higher caching values will enable faster scanners but will eat up more memory and some calls of next may take longer and longer times when the cache is empty. Do not set this value such that the time between invocations is greater than the scanner timeout; i.e. hbase.client.scanner.timeout.period",e.jsx(i.br,{}),`
`,e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Default:"})," ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"2147483647"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(i.h4,{id:"hbaseclientkeyvaluemaxsize-toc",children:e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.client.keyvalue.maxsize"})}),`
