`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.rpc.timeout"})," property limits how long a single RPC call can run before timing out. To fine tune read or write related RPC timeouts set ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.rpc.read.timeout"})," and ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.rpc.write.timeout"})," configuration properties. In the absence of these properties ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.rpc.timeout"})," will be used."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["A higher-level timeout is ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.client.operation.timeout"})," which is valid for each client call. When an RPC call fails for instance for a timeout due to ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.rpc.timeout"})," it will be retried until ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.client.operation.timeout"})," is reached. Client operation timeout for system tables can be fine tuned by setting ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.client.meta.operation.timeout"})," configuration value. When this is not set its value will use ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.client.operation.timeout"}),"."]}),`
