`,e.jsx(i.h4,{id:"region-server-memory-consumption-changes-toc",children:"Region Server memory consumption changes."}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Users upgrading from versions prior to HBase 1.4 should read the instructions in section ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"/docs/upgrading/paths#region-server-memory-consumption-changes",children:"Region Server memory consumption changes."}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"Additionally, HBase 2.0 has changed how memstore memory is tracked for flushing decisions. Previously, both the data size and overhead for storage were used to calculate utilization against the flush threshold. Now, only data size is used to make these per-region decisions. Globally the addition of the storage overhead is used to make decisions about forced flushes."}),`
`,e.jsx(i.h4,{id:"web-ui-for-splitting-and-merging-operate-on-row-prefixes-toc",children:"Web UI for splitting and merging operate on row prefixes"}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"Previously, the Web UI included functionality on table status pages to merge or split based on an encoded region name. In HBase 2.0, instead this functionality works by taking a row prefix."}),`
`,e.jsx(i.h4,{id:"special-upgrading-for-replication-users-from-pre-hbase-14-toc",children:"Special upgrading for Replication users from pre-HBase 1.4"}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["User running versions of HBase prior to the 1.4.0 release that make use of replication should be sure to read the instructions in the section ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"/docs/upgrading/paths#replication-peers-tablecfs-config",children:"Replication peer's TableCFs config"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(i.h4,{id:"hbase-shell-changes-toc",children:"HBase shell changes"}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"The HBase shell command relies on a bundled JRuby instance. This bundled JRuby been updated from version 1.6.8 to version 9.1.10.0. The represents a change from Ruby 1.8 to Ruby 2.3.3, which introduces non-compatible language changes for user scripts."}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"The HBase shell command now ignores the '--return-values' flag that was present in early HBase 1.4 releases. Instead the shell always behaves as though that flag were passed. If you wish to avoid having expression results printed in the console you should alter your IRB configuration."}),`
`,e.jsx(i.h4,{id:"coprocessor-apis-have-changed-in-hbase-20-toc",children:"Coprocessor APIs have changed in HBase 2.0+"}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["All Coprocessor APIs have been refactored to improve supportability around binary API compatibility for future versions of HBase. If you or applications you rely on have custom HBase coprocessors, you should read ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/HBASE-18169",children:"the release notes for HBASE-18169"})," for details of changes you will need to make prior to upgrading to HBase 2.0+."]}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"For example, if you had a BaseRegionObserver in HBase 1.2 then at a minimum you will need to update it to implement both RegionObserver and RegionCoprocessor and add the method"}),`
