`,e.jsx(i.h2,{id:"tls",children:"Transport Level Security (TLS) in HBase RPC communication"}),`
`,e.jsxs(e.Fragment,{children:[e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Since version ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"2.6.0"})," HBase supports TLS encryption in server-client and Master-RegionServer communication. ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transport_Layer_Security",children:"Transport Layer Security (TLS)"})," is a standard cryptographic protocol designed to provide communications security over a computer network. HBase TLS implementation works exactly how secure websites are accessed via ",e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"https"})," prefix in a web browser: once established all communication on the channel will be securely hidden from malicious access."]}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"The encryption works at the transport level which means it's independent of the configured authentication method. Secure client access mentioned in the previous section requires Kerberos to be configured and used in HBase authentication, while TLS can be configured with any other SASL mechanism or even with simple client access methods, effectively preventing attackers from eavesdropping the communication. No Kerberos KDC or other complicated infrastructure required."}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"HBase TLS is based on the Netty library therefore it only works with Netty client and server RPC implementations. Netty's powerful SSL implementation is a great foundation for highly secure and performant communication providing the latest and greatest cryptographic solution at all times."}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"Since Region Servers effectively work as clients from Master's perspective, TLS supports encrypted communication between cluster members too."}),`
