`,e.jsxs(i.li,{children:[e.jsx(i.em,{children:"hbase.client.bootstrap.initial_refresh_delay_secs"}),": the initial refresh interval in seconds, the default value is 1/10 of ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"hbase.client.bootstrap.refresh_interval_secs"}),". The reason why we want to introduce a separated configuration for the delay for first refreshing is that, as end users could configure any nodes in a cluster as the initial bootstrap nodes, it is possible that different end users will configure the same machine which makes the machine over load. So we should have a shorter delay for the initial refresh, to let users quickly switch to the bootstrap nodes we want them to connect to."]}),`
