`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"HFile"})," file format is based on the SSTable file described in the ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"http://research.google.com/archive/bigtable.html",children:"BigTable [2006"}),"] paper and on Hadoop's ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://hadoop.apache.org/docs/current/api/org/apache/hadoop/io/file/tfile/TFile.html",children:"TFile"})," (The unit test suite and the compression harness were taken directly from TFile). Schubert Zhang's blog post on ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"http://cloudepr.blogspot.com/2009/09/hfile-block-indexed-file-format-to.html",children:"HFile: A Block-Indexed File Format to Store Sorted Key-Value Pairs"})," makes for a thorough introduction to HBase's HFile. Matteo Bertozzi has also put up a helpful description, ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"http://th30z.blogspot.com/2011/02/hbase-io-hfile.html?spref=tw",children:"HBase I/O: HFile"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["For more information, see the HFile source code. Also see ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"/docs/hfile-format#hbase-file-format-with-inline-blocks-version-2",children:"HBase file format with inline blocks (version 2)"})," for information about the HFile v2 format that was included in 0.92."]}),`
