`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"The key points here is to keep all these pauses low. CMS pauses are always low, but if your ParNew starts growing, you can see minor GC pauses approach 100ms, exceed 100ms and hit as high at 400ms."}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"This can be due to the size of the ParNew, which should be relatively small. If your ParNew is very large after running HBase for a while, in one example a ParNew was about 150MB, then you might have to constrain the size of ParNew (The larger it is, the longer the collections take but if it's too small, objects are promoted to old gen too quickly). In the below we constrain new gen size to 64m."}),`
