`,e.jsx(i.li,{children:'For connectivity issues, usually an exception like "MasterRegistryFetchException: Exception making rpc to masters..." is logged in the client logs. The logging includes the list of master end points that were attempted by the client. The bottom part of the stack trace should include the underlying reason. If you suspect connectivity issues (ConnectionRefused?), make sure the master end points are accessible from client.'}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.li,{children:["If there is a suspicion of higher load on the masters due to hedging of RPCs, it can be controlled by either reducing the hedging fan out (via ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"hbase.rpc.hedged.fanout"}),") or by restricting the set of masters that clients can access for the master registry purposes (via ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"hbase.masters"}),")."]}),`
