`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["The default behavior is to perform a flush of data in memory before the snapshot is taken. This means that data in memory is included in the snapshot. In most cases, this is the desired behavior. However, if your set-up can tolerate data in memory being excluded from the snapshot, you can use the ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"SKIP_FLUSH"})," option of the ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"snapshot"})," command to disable and flushing while taking the snapshot."]}),`
