`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Optionally, snapshots can be created with a custom max file size configuration that will be used by cloned tables, instead of the global ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.hregion.max.filesize"})," configuration property. This is mostly useful when exporting snapshots between different clusters. If the HBase cluster where the snapshot is originally taken has a much larger value set for ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.hregion.max.filesize"})," than one or more clusters where the snapshot is being exported to, a storm of region splits may occur when restoring the snapshot on destination clusters. Specifying ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"MAX_FILESIZE"})," on properties passed to ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"snapshot"})," command will save informed value into the table's ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"MAX_FILESIZE"})," decriptor at snapshot creation time. If the table already defines ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"MAX_FILESIZE"})," descriptor, this property would be ignored and have no effect."]}),`
