`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["High level, you create a rsgroup that is other than the ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"default"})," group using ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"add_rsgroup"})," command. You then add servers and tables to this group with the ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"move_servers_rsgroup"})," and ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"move_tables_rsgroup"})," commands. If necessary, run a balance for the group if tables are slow to migrate to the groups dedicated server with the ",e.jsx(i.em,{children:"balance_rsgroup"})," command (Usually this is not needed). To monitor effect of the commands, see the ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"Tables"})," tab toward the end of the Master UI home page. If you click on a table, you can see what servers it is deployed across. You should see here a reflection of the grouping done with your shell commands. View the master log if issues."]}),`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"Here is example using a few of the rsgroup commands. To add a group, do as follows:"}),`
