`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["When enabled, Normalizer is invoked in the background every 5 mins (by default), which can be configured using ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase.normalization.period"})," in ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"hbase-site.xml"}),". Normalizer can also be invoked manually/programmatically at will using HBase shell's ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"normalize"})," command. HBase by default uses ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"SimpleRegionNormalizer"}),", but users can design their own normalizer as long as they implement the RegionNormalizer Interface. Details about the logic used by ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"SimpleRegionNormalizer"})," to compute its normalization plan can be found ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://hbase.apache.org/devapidocs/org/apache/hadoop/hbase/master/normalizer/SimpleRegionNormalizer.html",children:"here"}),"."]}),`
